            "count": 0,
            "bug_id": 19325,
            "text": "Created attachment 4076\nPatch that fixes the bug\n\n#Steps to reproduce\nMake a fresh install of R-4.6.2 (binary version) on Windows 10 x64 bits\nThe bug is also found in R-devel (2026-11-15 r90890)\nRun c:\\program files\\R-4.6.2\\bin\\x64\\Rgui.exe\ncopy/paste the following commands in the console\nwinMenuAdd(\"Testit\")\nwinMenuAddItem(\"Testit\", \"one\", \"short\")\nwinMenuAddItem(\"Testit\", \"one\", \"this is a longer string\")\nwinMenuAddItem(\"Testit\", \"one\", \"check allocator\")\n\n#Diagnostic\nI opened the WinDbg crash dump in %localappdata%\\CrashDumps and opened it with WinDbgTool and found that the culprit is a call to realloc() in winaddmenuitem.\nSTACK_TEXT:  \n00007ff8`f5139808 00007ff8`f507a505 ntdll!RtlpLogHeapFailure+0x45\n00007ff8`f5139810 00007ff8`f5088f43 ntdll!RtlpReAllocateHeapInternal+0x95203\n00007ff8`f5139818 00007ff8`f4ff3d1a ntdll!RtlReAllocateHeap+0x5a\n00007ff8`f5139820 00007ff8`81ff82e1 aclayers!NS_FaultTolerantHeap::APIHook_RtlReAllocateHeap+0x7e1\n00007ff8`f5139828 00007ff8`f13a4e09 ucrtbase!_realloc_base+0x39\n00007ff8`f5139830 00007ff8`7f80ae5a r!winaddmenuitem+0x18a\n00007ff8`f5139838 00007ff8`7f7b03b2 utils!winMenuAdd+0x132\n00007ff8`f5139840 00007ff8`7fa2048f r!rwarn_+0x2299f\n00007ff8`f5139848 00007ff8`7f8e4ab8 r!R_ParseEvalString+0x8248\n00007ff8`f5139850 00007ff8`7f8ef6eb r!R_ParseEvalString+0x12e7b\n00007ff8`f5139858 00007ff8`7f8ef9db r!R_ParseEvalString+0x1316b\n00007ff8`f5139860 00007ff8`7f8f49c2 r!Rf_eval+0x4922\n00007ff8`f5139868 00007ff8`7f8f5d7f r!Rf_eval+0x5cdf\n00007ff8`f5139870 00007ff8`7f8efbed r!R_ParseEvalString+0x1337d\n00007ff8`f5139878 00007ff8`7f91c0d0 r!Rf_ReplIteration+0x140\n00007ff8`f5139880 00007ff8`7f91c550 r!Rf_ReplIteration+0x5c0\n00007ff8`f5139888 00007ff8`7f91c5f2 r!run_Rmainloop+0x52\n00007ff8`f5139890 00007ff8`7f91c63e r!Rf_mainloop+0xe\n00007ff8`f5139898 00007ff6`4e4b1546 rgui+0x1546\n00007ff8`f51398a0 00007ff6`4e4b1476 rgui+0x1476\n00007ff8`f51398a8 00007ff6`4e4b12ee rgui+0x12ee\n00007ff8`f51398b0 00007ff6`4e4b13e6 rgui+0x13e6\n00007ff8`f51398b8 00007ff8`f4f04034 kernel32!BaseThreadInitThunk+0x14\n00007ff8`f51398c0 00007ff8`f5053691 ntdll!RtlUserThreadStart+0x21\n\nI opened the source code file src/gnuwin32/rui.c and, after a few tests, I understood that the bug comes from the fact that, when realloc() moves the memory, the original pointer (umitems[i]->action) is not updated, and so becomes a dangling pointer.\n\n#Bugfix\nWith the help of Rtools 4.5, I wrote a trivial patch and tested it on Windows.\nWithout the patch, the bug is reproducible on a fresh R-4.6.2 built on my machine with Rtools 4.5, but due to the fact that it relies on the specific allocator and the detection of a dangling pointer by the malloc heap allocator, it may not be reproducible on other machines with a different allocator or maybe even debug setting.\nWith my patch, the bug disappears on my machine.\n\n\n#Exact setting\nplatform       x86_64-w64-mingw32               \narch           x86_64                           \nos             mingw32                          \ncrt            ucrt                             \nsystem         x86_64, mingw32                  \nstatus                                          \nmajor          4                                \nminor          6.2                              \nyear           2026                             \nmonth          10                               \nday            29                               \nsvn rev        90784                            \nlanguage       R                                \nversion.string R version 4.6.2 (2026-10-29 ucrt)\nnickname       Diversified Portfolio  \n\nVersions of important system components:\nucrtbase.dll 10.0.17134.677\nWindows 10 Version 10.0.17134\n\nCPU: AMD Ryzen 7 1700\nMotherboard: AX370-Gaming K5",
            "attachment_id": 4076,
            "time": "2026-11-15T21:30:20Z",
            "creator": "Andre.Gillibert",
            "is_markdown": true
