            "attachment_id": {},
            "text": "#Reproducing on Wine\nI also tried to reproduce the Bug on Ubuntu 26.04 with wine and got the following error (standard installation of R-4.6.2):\n> winMenuAdd(\"Testit\")\n> winMenuAddItem(\"Testit\", \"one\", \"short\")\n> winMenuAddItem(\"Testit\", \"one\", \"this is a longer string\")\n> winMenuAddItem(\"Testit\", \"one\", \"check allocator\")\nError in .External2(C_winMenuAdd, menuname, itemname, action) : \n  unable to add menu item (failed to allocate char storage)\n\nThis can be explained by the fact that the Wine heap allocator returns NULL when reallocating a dangling pointer and src/gnuwin32/rui.c emits an error in that case. The patch also fixes the bug on Wine.\n\n#Linux system information\n$ uname -a\nLinux ryzen 7.0.0-43-generic #43-Ubuntu SMP PREEMPT_DYNAMIC Fri Oct 23 13:25:25 UTC 2026 x86_64 GNU/Linux\n$ wine --version\nwine-10.0 (Ubuntu 10.0~repack-12ubuntu1)\n\n#R version\n               _                                \nplatform       x86_64-w64-mingw32               \narch           x86_64                           \nos             mingw32                          \ncrt            ucrt                             \nsystem         x86_64, mingw32                  \nstatus                                          \nmajor          4                                \nminor          6.2                              \nyear           2026                             \nmonth          10                               \nday            29                               \nsvn rev        90784                            \nlanguage       R                                \nversion.string R version 4.6.2 (2026-10-29 ucrt)\nnickname       Diversified Portfolio",
            "bug_id": 19325,
            "count": 1,
            "is_markdown": true,
