            "creator": "ikrylov",
            "bug_id": 19325,
            "text": "Thank you for the report!\n\nOn Windows Server 2022, I got the same error you got on Wine. Indeed, `realloc()` must be returning a null pointer in this case because it has already deallocated the `\"short\"` string:\n\n```\n1500                p = realloc(p, strlen(action) + 1);\n(gdb) p p\n$11 = 0x16aff7c0 \"short\"\n(gdb) n\n1501                if(!p) {\n(gdb) p p\n$12 = 0x0\n(gdb) p (void*)realloc((void*)0x16aff7c0, (size_t)strlen(\"check allocator\")+1)\n$16 = (void *) 0x0\n```\nThe code needs to remember the pointer newly returned by `realloc()`. I confirm that your patch fixes the problem.",
            "is_markdown": true,
            "count": 3,
            "attachment_id": {},
            "tags": [],
